WEBVTT

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.826
<i>Kristin: hey, meredith, it's kristin.</i>

00:03:15.859 --> 00:03:18.036
<i>You have to tell me
what happened last night.</i>

00:03:18.069 --> 00:03:19.040
<i>Call me.</i>

00:03:20.246 --> 00:03:22.389
<i>Brad: hey, meredith. Brad calling.</i>

00:03:22.422 --> 00:03:25.235
<i>Listen, do you want to hook up later?</i>

00:03:25.268 --> 00:03:28.617
<i>Well, i'll talk to you
then. Give me a call. Thanks.</i>

00:03:33.237 --> 00:03:35.715
<i>Brock: hey, meredith, what's
going on? This is brock.</i>

00:03:35.747 --> 00:03:38.561
<i>I just wanted to let you know
the gang is gonna get together.</i>

00:03:38.594 --> 00:03:40.402
<i>We're gonna go to the garage.</i>

00:03:40.435 --> 00:03:42.444
<i>We're gonna have some
beers and some shots.</i>

00:04:13.113 --> 00:04:16.093
All right, dean, this is the place.

00:04:16.126 --> 00:04:18.102
I've got to say dad and me did just fine

00:04:18.135 --> 00:04:20.479
Without these stupid costumes.

00:04:20.513 --> 00:04:23.828
I feel like a
high-School-Drama dork.

00:04:25.702 --> 00:04:27.678
What was that play that you did?

00:04:27.711 --> 00:04:29.519
What was it
-- "Our town"?

00:04:29.553 --> 00:04:31.193
Yeah, you were good. It was cute.

00:04:31.227 --> 00:04:33.034
Look, you want to pull this off or not?

00:04:33.068 --> 00:04:35.579
I'm just saying these outfits
cost hard-Earned money.

00:04:35.613 --> 00:04:36.684
Whose?

00:04:36.718 --> 00:04:40.065
Ours. You think
credit-Card fraud is easy?

00:04:42.342 --> 00:04:44.318
Thanks for letting us look around.

00:04:44.351 --> 00:04:47.868
The police said they were
done with the place, so...

00:04:58.548 --> 00:05:00.690
You guys said you were
with the alarm company?

00:05:00.725 --> 00:05:02.063
That's right.

00:05:02.098 --> 00:05:03.369
Well, no offense,

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:06.549
But your alarm is about as
useful as boobs on a man.

00:05:06.583 --> 00:05:08.558
Well, that's
why we're here --

00:05:08.592 --> 00:05:11.940
To see what went wrong, to
stop it from happening again.

00:05:13.983 --> 00:05:15.791
Now, ma'am, you found the body?

00:05:15.824 --> 00:05:16.962
Yeah.

00:05:16.997 --> 00:05:18.301
Right after it happened?

00:05:18.335 --> 00:05:19.641
No, a few days later.

00:05:19.674 --> 00:05:22.319
Meredith's work called.
She hadn't showed up.

00:05:22.352 --> 00:05:24.429
I knocked on her door.

00:05:24.463 --> 00:05:27.409
That's when i noticed... the smell.

00:05:27.442 --> 00:05:30.891
Any windows open? Any sign of break-In?

00:05:30.924 --> 00:05:32.364
Windows were locked.
Front door was bolted.

00:05:32.397 --> 00:05:34.775
Chain was on the door. We
had to cut it to get in.

00:05:34.808 --> 00:05:36.114
And the alarm was still on?

00:05:36.148 --> 00:05:39.128
Like i said. Bang-Up job
your company is doing.

00:05:39.162 --> 00:05:41.237
Did you see any overturned furniture,

00:05:41.271 --> 00:05:42.911
Broken glass, signs of struggle?

00:05:42.944 --> 00:05:45.891
Everything was in perfect condition...

00:05:45.925 --> 00:05:47.833
Except meredith.

00:05:47.866 --> 00:05:51.013
Well, what condition was meredith in?

00:05:51.047 --> 00:05:54.428
Meredith was all over, in pieces.

00:05:54.461 --> 00:05:57.308
The guy who killed her
must have been a whack job.

00:05:57.342 --> 00:05:59.920
But i tell you, if i
didn't know any better,

00:05:59.953 --> 00:06:02.163
I'd have said a wild animal did it.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:07.821
Ma'am, you mind if we take some time,

00:06:07.855 --> 00:06:09.931
Give this place a once-Over?

00:06:09.964 --> 00:06:13.379
Go right ahead. Knock yourself out.

00:06:18.803 --> 00:06:20.946
So the killer walks in
and out of the apartment --

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.453
No weapons, no prints, nothing.

00:06:22.486 --> 00:06:24.796
I'm telling you, the
minute i found that article,

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:26.471
I knew this was our kind of gig.

00:06:26.503 --> 00:06:28.011
I think i agree with you.

00:06:28.044 --> 00:06:30.521
So, you talked to the cops?

00:06:30.554 --> 00:06:34.071
Uh, yeah, i
spoke to amy --

00:06:34.104 --> 00:06:38.089
A, uh, charming, perky
officer of the law.

00:06:38.122 --> 00:06:39.429
What did you find out?

00:06:39.462 --> 00:06:42.442
Well, she's a sagittarius.
She loves tequila.

00:06:42.475 --> 00:06:44.651
I mean...whew.

00:06:44.684 --> 00:06:46.827
Oh, and she's got this
little tattoo. Dean!

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:47.999
What? Yeah.

00:06:48.033 --> 00:06:49.841
Nothing we don't already know,

00:06:49.874 --> 00:06:53.155
Except for one thing they're
keeping out of the papers.

00:06:53.188 --> 00:06:54.628
Meredith's heart was missing.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:57.609
Her heart?

00:06:57.641 --> 00:07:00.119
Yeah, her heart.

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:01.960
So, what do you think did it to her?

00:07:01.994 --> 00:07:04.372
The landlady said it looked
like an animal attack.

00:07:04.405 --> 00:07:07.285
Maybe it was. Werewolf?

00:07:07.318 --> 00:07:09.193
Not a werewolf. The
lunar cycle's not right.

00:07:09.227 --> 00:07:10.264
If it was a creature,

00:07:10.298 --> 00:07:12.072
It would've left some kind of trace.

00:07:12.105 --> 00:07:15.754
It was probably a spirit.

00:07:15.789 --> 00:07:17.898
Hmm.

00:07:17.931 --> 00:07:21.448
See if you can find
any masking tape around.

00:07:44.147 --> 00:07:46.458
Ever see that symbol before?

00:07:46.492 --> 00:07:48.935
Never.

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:50.944
Me, neither.

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:26.770
I talked to the bartender.

00:08:26.803 --> 00:08:29.214
Did you get anything...
besides her number?

00:08:29.247 --> 00:08:33.097
Dude, i'm a professional.
I'm offended that...

00:08:34.738 --> 00:08:37.350
All right.

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:39.559
You mind doing a little bit of thinking

00:08:39.594 --> 00:08:41.401
With your upstairs brain, dean?

00:08:41.435 --> 00:08:43.141
Hmm? There's nothing to find out.

00:08:43.175 --> 00:08:45.184
Meredith worked here. She waited tables.

00:08:45.218 --> 00:08:47.730
Everyone here is her friend.
Everyone says she's normal.

00:08:47.763 --> 00:08:50.073
She didn't do or say anything
weird before she died.

00:08:50.107 --> 00:08:52.349
What about that symbol?
Did you find anything?

00:08:52.383 --> 00:08:53.756
Nope. Nothing.

00:08:53.789 --> 00:08:56.266
It wasn't in dad's journal
or in any of the usual books.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:59.047
I just have to dig a
little deeper, i guess.

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:02.461
There was a first victim,
right, before meredith?

00:09:02.494 --> 00:09:04.470
Right, yeah. His name was, uh...

00:09:04.503 --> 00:09:06.512
His name was ben swardstrom.

00:09:06.546 --> 00:09:09.192
Last month he was found
mutilated in his town house.

00:09:09.224 --> 00:09:12.270
Same deal. The door was
locked. The alarm was on.

00:09:12.304 --> 00:09:14.214
Is there any connection between them?

00:09:14.246 --> 00:09:15.552
Nothing i could tell.

00:09:15.586 --> 00:09:17.595
Ben was a banker.
Meredith was a waitress.

00:09:17.628 --> 00:09:19.704
They never met, never
knew anyone in common.

00:09:19.737 --> 00:09:22.082
They were practically
from different worlds.

00:09:22.115 --> 00:09:23.923
So the only successful
intel we've scored

00:09:23.956 --> 00:09:26.635
Is the bartender's phone number.

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:29.950
What?

00:09:32.996 --> 00:09:34.168
Sam?

00:09:42.571 --> 00:09:43.711
Meg.

00:09:43.744 --> 00:09:45.318
Sam!

00:09:49.603 --> 00:09:53.821
Sam, is that you? Oh, my gosh!

00:09:55.629 --> 00:09:58.643
What are you doing here?

00:09:58.676 --> 00:10:00.618
I'm just in town
-- Visiting friends.

00:10:02.593 --> 00:10:03.732
Where are they?

00:10:03.765 --> 00:10:06.077
Well, they're not here right now,

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:07.683
But what about you, meg?

00:10:07.716 --> 00:10:09.559
I thought you were going to california.

00:10:09.591 --> 00:10:10.897
Oh, i did.

00:10:10.931 --> 00:10:13.108
I came. I saw. I conquered.

00:10:13.141 --> 00:10:15.651
Oh, and i met
what's his name --

00:10:15.685 --> 00:10:18.163
Something michael
murray -- At a bar.

00:10:18.196 --> 00:10:19.335
Who?

00:10:19.368 --> 00:10:20.608
It doesn't matter.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:23.018
Anyway, the whole scene got old,

00:10:23.051 --> 00:10:25.328
So i'm living here for a while.

00:10:26.567 --> 00:10:27.872
You're from chicago?

00:10:27.906 --> 00:10:30.885
No, massachusetts
-- Andover.

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:32.459
Gosh, sam,

00:10:32.493 --> 00:10:34.670
What are the odds we'd
run into each other?

00:10:34.702 --> 00:10:36.679
I know. I thought i'd
never see you again.

00:10:36.711 --> 00:10:38.955
Well, i'm glad you were wrong.

00:10:42.403 --> 00:10:44.412
Dude, cover your mouth.

00:10:44.446 --> 00:10:47.325
Yeah, i'm sorry, meg.

00:10:47.359 --> 00:10:50.574
This is, um -- This
is my brother, dean.

00:10:52.616 --> 00:10:53.820
This is dean?

00:10:53.854 --> 00:10:55.629
Yeah. So you've heard of me?

00:10:55.663 --> 00:10:57.470
Oh, yeah, i've heard of you.

00:10:57.504 --> 00:11:01.287
Nice -- The way you treat
your brother like luggage.

00:11:01.321 --> 00:11:02.627
Sorry?

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:05.237
Why don't you let him
do what he wants to do?

00:11:05.272 --> 00:11:07.682
Stop dragging him
over god's green earth.

00:11:07.716 --> 00:11:09.891
Meg...it's all right.

00:11:12.235 --> 00:11:15.383
Okay. Awkward.

00:11:15.417 --> 00:11:18.463
I'm gonna get a drink now.

00:11:23.049 --> 00:11:24.356
Sam, i'm sorry.

00:11:24.389 --> 00:11:29.076
It's just, the way you
told me he treats you,

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:30.951
If it were me, i'd kill him.

00:11:30.984 --> 00:11:32.492
It's all right. He means well.

00:11:32.525 --> 00:11:35.137
We should hook up while you're in town.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:36.309
Yeah.

00:11:36.342 --> 00:11:38.351
I could show you a hell of a time.

00:11:38.384 --> 00:11:39.657
That sounds great.

00:11:39.691 --> 00:11:41.666
Why don't you give me your number?

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:45.014

312-555-0143.

00:11:45.047 --> 00:11:46.890
You know what? I never
got your last name.

00:11:46.923 --> 00:11:48.530
Masters. Masters?

00:11:48.563 --> 00:11:49.769
So you better call.

00:11:49.802 --> 00:11:51.778
Scout's honor.

00:11:51.811 --> 00:11:55.828
I hope to see you around, sam.

00:12:05.371 --> 00:12:06.677
Who the hell we he?

00:12:06.711 --> 00:12:08.685
I don't really know.
I only met her once.

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:11.030
Meeting up with her again?

00:12:11.063 --> 00:12:14.378
I don't know, man. It's weird.

00:12:14.411 --> 00:12:17.056
What was she saying --
I treat you like luggage?

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:19.065
Were you bitching
about me to some chick?

00:12:19.099 --> 00:12:20.404
Look, i'm sorry, dean.

00:12:20.437 --> 00:12:21.911
It was when we had that huge fight

00:12:21.944 --> 00:12:23.953
When i was in the bus stop in indiana.

00:12:23.987 --> 00:12:25.962
Is there any truth to what she's saying?

00:12:25.996 --> 00:12:27.837
Am i keeping you against your will, sam?

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:29.779
No, of course not.
Now, would you listen?

00:12:29.813 --> 00:12:31.788
What?!

00:12:31.822 --> 00:12:34.299
I think there's something
strange going on here, dean.

00:12:34.332 --> 00:12:35.940
Tell me about it. She
wasn't even into me.

00:12:35.973 --> 00:12:38.517
No, man, i mean, like
our kind of strange.

00:12:38.551 --> 00:12:40.526
Maybe even a lead. Why do you say that?

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:43.339
I met meg weeks ago literally
on the side of the road.

00:12:43.372 --> 00:12:45.649
Now i run into her in
some random chicago bar --

00:12:45.682 --> 00:12:47.190
The same bar where a waitress

00:12:47.223 --> 00:12:49.266
Was slaughtered by
something supernatural.

00:12:49.298 --> 00:12:51.241
You don't think that's
weird? It happens.

00:12:51.275 --> 00:12:53.316
Well, yeah, it happens, but not to us.

00:12:53.349 --> 00:12:54.555
Look, i could be wrong.

00:12:54.589 --> 00:12:56.933
I'm just saying there's
something about this girl

00:12:56.966 --> 00:12:58.606
That i can't quite put my finger on.

00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:00.281
But i bet you'd like to.

00:13:00.315 --> 00:13:01.988
But maybe she's not a suspect.

00:13:02.022 --> 00:13:03.930
Maybe you got a thing for her, huh?

00:13:03.964 --> 00:13:07.279
You're thinking too much
with your upstairs brain, huh?

00:13:07.312 --> 00:13:09.355
Do me a favor.

00:13:09.387 --> 00:13:12.568
Check and see if there's a
meg masters from massachusetts

00:13:12.601 --> 00:13:15.046
And see if you can't dig
anything up on that symbol.

00:13:15.079 --> 00:13:16.519
What are you gonna do?

00:13:16.552 --> 00:13:18.328
I'm gonna watch meg.

00:13:18.361 --> 00:13:19.767
Yeah.

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:21.341
I just want to see what's what.

00:13:21.374 --> 00:13:22.881
All right, you little pervert.

00:13:22.914 --> 00:13:24.923
I'm going. I'm going.

00:13:49.197 --> 00:13:50.503
Hey.

00:13:50.537 --> 00:13:52.412
You're lurking outside
that poor girl's apartment,

00:13:52.446 --> 00:13:54.220
Aren't you? No.

00:13:55.759 --> 00:13:57.568
Yes.

00:13:57.601 --> 00:13:59.710
You've got a funny way
of showing your affection.

00:13:59.743 --> 00:14:02.423
You find anything on her or what?

00:14:02.456 --> 00:14:04.432
There's a meg masters in
the andover phone book.

00:14:04.465 --> 00:14:06.474
I even pulled up her high-School photo.

00:14:06.508 --> 00:14:08.650
Now, look, why don't
you go knock on her door

00:14:08.683 --> 00:14:10.994
And invite her to a poetry reading

00:14:11.027 --> 00:14:13.505
Or whatever it is you do, huh?

00:14:13.539 --> 00:14:15.581
What about the symbol? Any luck?

00:14:15.614 --> 00:14:17.890
Yeah, that i did have some luck with.

00:14:17.925 --> 00:14:21.908
Turns out it's zoroastrian.

00:14:21.942 --> 00:14:24.788
Very, very old-School, like
2,000 years before christ.

00:14:24.821 --> 00:14:26.295
It's a sigil for a daeva.

00:14:26.329 --> 00:14:27.767
What's a daeva?

00:14:27.801 --> 00:14:29.776
It translates to
"demon of darkness" --

00:14:29.810 --> 00:14:32.120
Zoroastrian demons, and
they're savage, animalistic,

00:14:32.154 --> 00:14:35.971
Nasty attitudes -- Kind
of like demonic pit bulls.

00:14:36.005 --> 00:14:38.180
How did you figure that out?

00:14:38.214 --> 00:14:40.324
You don't have a corner on
paper chasing around here.

00:14:40.357 --> 00:14:41.796
Name the last book you read.

00:14:43.838 --> 00:14:46.317
I called dad's friend
caleb. He told me, all right.

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:47.757
Anyway, here's the thing.

00:14:47.791 --> 00:14:50.033
These daevas, they have to be summoned.

00:14:50.067 --> 00:14:51.741
So someone's controlling it?

00:14:51.774 --> 00:14:53.247
Yeah, that's what i'm saying.

00:14:53.281 --> 00:14:55.792
And from what i gather, it's
pretty risky business, too.

00:14:55.826 --> 00:14:58.236
These suckers tend to bite
the hand that feeds them...

00:14:58.269 --> 00:15:00.781
And the arms and the torsos.

00:15:00.815 --> 00:15:01.986
What do they look like?

00:15:02.019 --> 00:15:04.162
Nobody's seen them for
a couple of millennia.

00:15:04.195 --> 00:15:05.804
Summoning a demon that ancient,

00:15:05.837 --> 00:15:07.544
Someone really knows their stuff.

00:15:07.577 --> 00:15:09.420
I think we've got a
major player in town.

00:15:10.893 --> 00:15:13.538
Why don't you go give that
girl a private strip-O-Gram?

00:15:13.571 --> 00:15:15.345
<i>Bite me. Bite her.</i>

00:15:15.379 --> 00:15:17.253
Don't leave teeth marks, though.

00:15:17.287 --> 00:15:19.262
Sam? Are
you --

00:15:48.559 --> 00:15:49.932
No, no,
i'm just --

00:15:49.966 --> 00:15:51.840
Pervert!

00:15:51.874 --> 00:15:54.485
What a creep!

00:18:49.292 --> 00:18:51.603
I don't think you should come

00:18:51.637 --> 00:18:54.449
Because the brothers
-- They're in town.

00:18:54.482 --> 00:18:56.157
I didn't
know that --

00:19:01.312 --> 00:19:02.618
Yes, sir.

00:19:02.652 --> 00:19:08.143
Yes, i'll be here... waiting for you.

00:20:32.818 --> 00:20:35.965
What the hell?

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:44.134
Dude, i've got to talk to you.

00:20:44.168 --> 00:20:46.344
So, hot little meg is
summoning the daeva?

00:20:46.378 --> 00:20:48.621
It looks like she was
using that black altar

00:20:48.655 --> 00:20:49.960
To control the thing.

00:20:49.995 --> 00:20:52.304
So sammy's got a thing for the bad girl.

00:20:52.337 --> 00:20:54.280
And what's the deal
with that bowl again?

00:20:54.313 --> 00:20:56.121
She was talking
into it --

00:20:56.154 --> 00:20:58.263
The way witches used to
scry into crystal balls.

00:20:58.297 --> 00:20:59.904
She was communicating with someone.

00:20:59.939 --> 00:21:02.583
With the daeva? No, you said
those things were savages.

00:21:02.616 --> 00:21:04.894
No, this was someone different,

00:21:04.927 --> 00:21:07.236
Someone who's giving her orders,

00:21:07.270 --> 00:21:10.016
Someone who's coming to that warehouse.

00:21:19.056 --> 00:21:20.193
Holy crap.

00:21:20.227 --> 00:21:21.668
What?

00:21:21.701 --> 00:21:23.677
What i was gonna tell you earlier.

00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:26.187
I pulled a favor with my

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:28.665
Friend amy over at
the police department.

00:21:28.699 --> 00:21:31.242
Complete records of the two victims.

00:21:31.276 --> 00:21:32.984
We missed something the first time.

00:21:33.018 --> 00:21:35.663
What?

00:21:35.696 --> 00:21:39.212
The first victim
-- The old man?

00:21:39.245 --> 00:21:41.589
He spent his whole life in chicago,

00:21:41.622 --> 00:21:44.367
But look where he was
born. Lawrence, kansas.

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:45.707
Mm-Hmm.

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:47.616
Meredith -- The
second victim?

00:21:47.649 --> 00:21:49.457
It turns out she was adopted.

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:51.298
And guess where she's from?

00:21:58.698 --> 00:21:59.837
Holy crap.

00:21:59.870 --> 00:22:01.176
Yeah.

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:03.452
I mean, that is where
the demon killed mom.

00:22:05.194 --> 00:22:06.868
You think meg's tied up with the demon?

00:22:06.901 --> 00:22:09.346
I think it's a definite possibility.

00:22:09.378 --> 00:22:11.890
What's the significance of lawrence?

00:22:11.923 --> 00:22:13.564
And how do these daeva things fit in?

00:22:13.597 --> 00:22:15.908
I say we trash that
black altar, grab meg,

00:22:15.941 --> 00:22:18.686
And have ourselves a
friendly little interrogation.

00:22:18.719 --> 00:22:20.561
No, we can't. We shouldn't tip her off.

00:22:20.595 --> 00:22:22.704
We've got to stake out that warehouse.

00:22:22.737 --> 00:22:25.550
We've got to see who...or
what is showing up to meet her.

00:22:25.583 --> 00:22:26.890
I'll tell you one thing.

00:22:26.923 --> 00:22:29.601
I don't think we should do this alone.

00:22:32.012 --> 00:22:33.485
We think we've got a serious lead

00:22:33.518 --> 00:22:35.159
On the thing that killed mom.

00:22:35.193 --> 00:22:41.354
So, uh, this warehouse
-- It's 1435 west erie.

00:22:41.388 --> 00:22:43.028
Dad, if you get this,

00:22:43.061 --> 00:22:45.907
Get to chicago as soon as you can.

00:22:45.940 --> 00:22:47.580
Voice mail?

00:22:47.614 --> 00:22:48.920
Yeah.

00:22:50.125 --> 00:22:51.598
Jeez. What'd you get?

00:22:51.632 --> 00:22:54.712
I ransacked
that trunk --

00:22:54.746 --> 00:22:57.224
Holy water, y weapon
that i could think of.

00:22:57.257 --> 00:23:00.672
Exorcism rituals from about
a half-Dozen religions.

00:23:00.705 --> 00:23:03.786
I'm not sure what to expect,

00:23:03.819 --> 00:23:06.765
So i guess we should just
expect everything, huh?

00:23:14.902 --> 00:23:17.548
It's a big night.

00:23:17.581 --> 00:23:20.158
Yeah.

00:23:20.193 --> 00:23:21.464
You nervous?

00:23:21.498 --> 00:23:25.013
No. No, are you?

00:23:25.047 --> 00:23:27.224
No. No way.

00:23:35.661 --> 00:23:37.469
God, could you imagine if we actually

00:23:37.502 --> 00:23:39.176
Found that damn thing, that demon?

00:23:39.210 --> 00:23:41.286
Let's not get ahead of
ourselves, all right?

00:23:41.319 --> 00:23:46.106
I know. I'm just
saying... what if we did?

00:23:46.140 --> 00:23:49.154
What if this whole
thing was over tonight?

00:23:49.187 --> 00:23:51.330
Man, i'd sleep for a month,

00:23:51.364 --> 00:23:55.214
Go back to school,
just be a person again.

00:23:55.247 --> 00:23:57.290
You want to go back to school?

00:23:57.323 --> 00:23:59.935
Yeah, once we're done hunting the thing.

00:24:01.107 --> 00:24:03.685
Why? Is there something wrong with that?

00:24:03.718 --> 00:24:07.468
No, no, it's great. Good for you.

00:24:07.502 --> 00:24:11.084
I mean, what are you gonna
do when it's all over?

00:24:11.117 --> 00:24:13.226
It's never gonna be over.

00:24:13.261 --> 00:24:14.533
There's gonna be others.

00:24:14.566 --> 00:24:16.843
There's always gonna
be something to hunt.

00:24:16.877 --> 00:24:19.689
But there's got to be something
that you want for yourself.

00:24:19.722 --> 00:24:22.133
I don't want you to leave
the second this is over.

00:24:22.166 --> 00:24:26.050
Dude, what's your problem?

00:24:32.043 --> 00:24:35.056
Why do you think i drag
you everywhere, huh?

00:24:35.090 --> 00:24:38.304
Why do you think i came
and got you at stanford?

00:24:38.338 --> 00:24:40.582
'Cause dad was in trouble.

00:24:40.615 --> 00:24:43.259
'Cause you wanted to find
the thing that killed mom.

00:24:43.294 --> 00:24:45.436
Yes, that, but it's more than that, man.

00:24:51.999 --> 00:24:56.653
You and me
and dad --

00:24:56.686 --> 00:25:00.068
I want us to be together again.

00:25:02.044 --> 00:25:06.362
I want us to be a family again.

00:25:06.396 --> 00:25:11.084
<i>Dean, we are a family.
I'd do anything for you.</i>

00:25:11.117 --> 00:25:14.130
But things will never be
the way they were before.

00:25:19.755 --> 00:25:22.433
They could be.

00:25:26.150 --> 00:25:27.824
I don't want them to be.

00:25:32.009 --> 00:25:34.018
I'm not gonna live this life forever.

00:25:34.051 --> 00:25:37.399
Dean, when this is all over,

00:25:37.432 --> 00:25:40.681
You're gonna have to
let me go my own way.

00:26:43.726 --> 00:26:48.012
Guys. Hiding is a little bit
childish, don't you think?

00:26:48.046 --> 00:26:50.021
That didn't work out like i'd planned.

00:26:52.968 --> 00:26:53.168
Why don't you come out?

00:27:03.280 --> 00:27:06.795
Sam, i have to say,

00:27:06.828 --> 00:27:09.541
This puts a real crimp
in our relationship.

00:27:09.575 --> 00:27:11.416
Yeah, tell me about it.

00:27:11.449 --> 00:27:14.127
So, where's your little daeva friend?

00:27:14.162 --> 00:27:15.367
Around.

00:27:15.400 --> 00:27:18.045
And that shotgun's
not gonna do much good.

00:27:18.079 --> 00:27:19.987
Oh, don't worry, sweetheart.

00:27:20.020 --> 00:27:21.527
The shotgun's not for the demon.

00:27:21.561 --> 00:27:25.143
So, who is it, meg? Who's coming?

00:27:25.176 --> 00:27:26.651
Who are you waiting for?

00:27:26.684 --> 00:27:29.194
You.

00:27:59.580 --> 00:28:02.760
Hey, sam, don't take this the wrong way,

00:28:02.794 --> 00:28:06.141
But your girlfriend... is a bitch.

00:28:06.175 --> 00:28:10.360
This, the whole thing, was a trap.

00:28:12.268 --> 00:28:14.913
Running into you at the bar,

00:28:14.948 --> 00:28:18.664
Following you here, hearing
what you had to say --

00:28:18.697 --> 00:28:20.739
It was all a setup, wasn't it?

00:28:22.346 --> 00:28:24.355
And that the victims were from lawrence.

00:28:24.388 --> 00:28:25.762
It doesn't mean anything.

00:28:25.796 --> 00:28:28.406
It was just to draw you in, that's all.

00:28:28.440 --> 00:28:30.282
You killed those two people for nothing.

00:28:30.315 --> 00:28:32.592
Baby, i've killed a
lot more for a lot less.

00:28:34.500 --> 00:28:37.647
You trapped us. Good for you.

00:28:37.681 --> 00:28:39.992
It's miller time.

00:28:40.025 --> 00:28:41.833
Why don't you kill us already?

00:28:41.867 --> 00:28:44.981
Not very quick on the uptake, are we?

00:28:50.639 --> 00:28:52.312
This trap isn't for you.

00:28:56.197 --> 00:28:57.367
Dad.

00:28:58.540 --> 00:28:59.980
It's a trap for dad.

00:29:02.860 --> 00:29:05.705
Oh, sweetheart, you're
dumber than you look.

00:29:05.739 --> 00:29:09.689
'Cause even if dad was
in town, which he is not,

00:29:09.723 --> 00:29:11.698
He wouldn't walk into
something like this.

00:29:11.732 --> 00:29:13.439
He's too good.

00:29:13.473 --> 00:29:15.816
He is pretty good, i'll give you that.

00:29:20.838 --> 00:29:22.847
But you see

00:29:28.205 --> 00:29:30.013
He has one weakness.

00:29:30.046 --> 00:29:31.386
What's that?

00:29:31.419 --> 00:29:33.160
You.

00:29:34.566 --> 00:29:37.446
He lets his guard down around his boys,

00:29:37.480 --> 00:29:40.861
Lets his emotions cloud his judgment.

00:29:42.836 --> 00:29:45.648
<i>I happen to know he is in town,</i>

00:29:45.681 --> 00:29:50.437
And he'll come and try to save you.

00:29:50.471 --> 00:29:53.349
And then the daevas
will kill everybody --

00:29:53.383 --> 00:29:57.970
Nice and slow... and messy.

00:29:58.003 --> 00:30:00.314
Well, i've got news for you.

00:30:00.347 --> 00:30:03.661
It's gonna take a lot more
than some...shadow to kill him.

00:30:03.695 --> 00:30:05.872
Oh, the daevas are in the room here.

00:30:05.905 --> 00:30:07.110
They're invisible.

00:30:07.144 --> 00:30:09.488
Their shadows are just
the only part you can see.

00:30:09.522 --> 00:30:11.028
Why are you doing this, meg?

00:30:11.061 --> 00:30:13.272
What kind of deal you got
worked out here, huh...

00:30:13.305 --> 00:30:14.610
And with who?

00:30:14.645 --> 00:30:16.553
I'm doing this for the same reasons

00:30:16.586 --> 00:30:18.562
You do what
you do --

00:30:18.595 --> 00:30:20.938
Loyalty, love.

00:30:26.631 --> 00:30:28.606
Like the love you had for
mommy...and jess.Go to he

00:30:28.640 --> 00:30:32.188
Baby, i'm already there.

00:30:34.230 --> 00:30:36.374
Come on, sam.

00:30:36.407 --> 00:30:39.420
There's no need to be nasty.

00:30:43.939 --> 00:30:47.924
I think we both know...

00:30:47.957 --> 00:30:50.805
How you really feel about me.

00:30:54.252 --> 00:30:55.926
You know

00:30:58.002 --> 00:31:01.986
I saw you... watching me...

00:31:02.019 --> 00:31:05.569
Changing in my apartment.

00:31:05.603 --> 00:31:08.181
It turned you on, didn't it?

00:31:08.214 --> 00:31:10.223
Get a room, you two.

00:31:10.257 --> 00:31:11.764
I didn't mind.

00:31:11.798 --> 00:31:14.442
I liked that you were watching me.

00:31:14.476 --> 00:31:16.451
Come on, sammy,

00:31:16.484 --> 00:31:19.465
You and i can still
have a little dirty fun.

00:31:19.498 --> 00:31:22.108
You want to have fun? Go ahead, then.

00:31:22.142 --> 00:31:24.654
I'm a little tied up right now.

00:32:00.011 --> 00:32:02.990
Now, were you just trying to distract me

00:32:03.024 --> 00:32:06.170
While your brother cuts free?

00:32:06.204 --> 00:32:08.849
No.

00:32:08.883 --> 00:32:10.858
No.

00:32:10.892 --> 00:32:13.771
It was because i have a knife of my own.

00:32:16.483 --> 00:32:17.789
Sam!

00:32:17.823 --> 00:32:19.664
Get the altar.

00:32:59.507 --> 00:33:01.148
So, i guess the daevas

00:33:01.182 --> 00:33:03.491
Didn't like being bossed around.

00:33:03.524 --> 00:33:05.668
I guess not.

00:33:05.701 --> 00:33:07.007
Hey, sam?

00:33:07.041 --> 00:33:08.179
Hmm?

00:33:08.213 --> 00:33:10.188
Next time you want to get laid,

00:33:10.222 --> 00:33:13.904
Find a girl that's not
so buckets of crazy, huh?

00:33:28.770 --> 00:33:31.181
Why don't you just leave
that stuff in the car?

00:33:31.215 --> 00:33:33.524
I said it before, and
i'll say it again --

00:33:33.557 --> 00:33:36.738
Better safe than sorry.

00:33:40.321 --> 00:33:41.492
Hey!

00:33:54.450 --> 00:33:56.058
Dad.

00:33:56.091 --> 00:33:58.100
Hey, boys.

00:34:26.592 --> 00:34:27.730
Hi, sam.

00:34:27.764 --> 00:34:29.104
Hi, dad.

00:34:32.652 --> 00:34:34.963
Dad, it was a trap.

00:34:34.996 --> 00:34:38.646
I didn't know. I'm sorry.

00:34:38.679 --> 00:34:41.792
It's all right. I thought
it might have been.

00:34:41.827 --> 00:34:43.367
Were you there?

00:34:43.401 --> 00:34:47.753
I got there just in time to
see the girl take the swan dive.

00:34:47.786 --> 00:34:49.159
She was the bad guy, right?

00:34:49.193 --> 00:34:50.699
Yes, sir.Yes, sir.

00:34:50.732 --> 00:34:53.211
Good. Well, it doesn't surprise me.

00:34:53.244 --> 00:34:55.689
It's tried to stop me before.

00:34:55.754 --> 00:34:57.730
The demon has?

00:34:57.763 --> 00:35:01.079
It knows i'm close. It
knows i'm gonna kill it.

00:35:01.112 --> 00:35:04.695
Not just exorcise it
or send it back to hell,

00:35:04.729 --> 00:35:07.507
Actually kill it.

00:35:07.540 --> 00:35:09.114
How?

00:35:09.148 --> 00:35:12.228
I'm working on that.

00:35:12.261 --> 00:35:15.911
Let us come with you. We'll help.

00:35:15.944 --> 00:35:19.528
No, sam.

00:35:19.561 --> 00:35:20.598
Not yet.

00:35:20.632 --> 00:35:22.874
Listen, try to understand.

00:35:22.908 --> 00:35:25.353
This demon is a scary son of a bitch.

00:35:25.386 --> 00:35:28.031
I don't want you
caught in the crossfire.

00:35:28.064 --> 00:35:29.371
I don't want you hurt.

00:35:29.404 --> 00:35:31.547
You don't have to worry about us.

00:35:31.581 --> 00:35:32.585
Of course i do.

00:35:34.928 --> 00:35:36.937
I'm your father.

00:35:40.989 --> 00:35:45.308
Listen, sammy, the last
time we were together,

00:35:45.341 --> 00:35:47.149
We had one hell of a fight.

00:35:47.183 --> 00:35:48.321
Yes, sir.

00:35:56.223 --> 00:35:59.202
It's good to see you again.

00:35:59.236 --> 00:36:01.077
It's been a long time.

00:36:03.488 --> 00:36:04.828
Too long.

00:36:32.449 --> 00:36:33.957
No!

00:37:12.875 --> 00:37:14.751
These things are shadow demons,

00:37:14.784 --> 00:37:16.491
So let's light 'em up!

00:37:31.524 --> 00:37:32.663
Dad!

00:37:32.696 --> 00:37:33.902
Over here!

00:37:36.112 --> 00:37:38.355
Come on!

00:38:03.299 --> 00:38:05.609
All right, come on. We
don't have much time.

00:38:05.642 --> 00:38:08.120
As soon as the flare's
out, they'll be back.

00:38:08.154 --> 00:38:09.693
Wait, wait!

00:38:09.727 --> 00:38:12.105
Sam, wait.

00:38:15.754 --> 00:38:17.227
Dad, you can't come with us.

00:38:17.260 --> 00:38:22.485
What? What are you talking about?

00:38:22.518 --> 00:38:24.023
We'll be all right.

00:38:24.058 --> 00:38:26.836
Dean, we should stick together!
We'll go after those --

00:38:26.870 --> 00:38:28.209
Sam, listen to me!

00:38:31.156 --> 00:38:33.198
We almost got dad killed in there.

00:38:33.231 --> 00:38:36.211
Don't you understand?
They're not gonna stop.

00:38:36.245 --> 00:38:37.817
They're gonna try again.

00:38:37.852 --> 00:38:40.262
They're gonna use us to get to him.

00:38:40.296 --> 00:38:41.970
I mean, meg was right.

00:38:42.003 --> 00:38:44.815
Dad's vulnerable when he's with us.

00:38:46.424 --> 00:38:50.842
He...he's stronger without us around.

00:38:52.918 --> 00:38:54.593
Dad...

00:38:56.300 --> 00:38:58.276
No.

00:38:58.309 --> 00:39:00.419
After everything,

00:39:00.452 --> 00:39:03.197
After all the time we
spent looking for you,

00:39:03.231 --> 00:39:05.742
Please.

00:39:05.776 --> 00:39:07.517
I've got to be a part of this fight.

00:39:07.550 --> 00:39:09.526
Sammy, this fight is just starting,

00:39:09.559 --> 00:39:12.271
And we are all gonna
have a part to play.

00:39:12.304 --> 00:39:14.045
For now, you've got to trust me, son.

00:39:16.422 --> 00:39:20.374
Okay? You've got to let me go.

00:40:04.402 --> 00:40:06.544
Be careful, boys.

00:40:07.850 --> 00:40:09.692
Come on.

00:00:00.524 --> 00:00:02.031
